+# Decision evidence map
+
+Selective leads for SkillForge, checked 2026-11-07. Read the source before reusing a conclusion. This is neither a complete archive nor qualification of the current combined package. [Attempt index](../Improvements/Index.md) retains older history; [validation scope](ValidationSummary.md) separates release evidence and unsupported claims.
+
+| Present question | Evidence and observation | Applicability / decision implication |
+|---|---|---|
+| Does explicit alternative generation improve actual solutions? | [Real Prompting comparison](ExperimentMemory20261107/Sources/RealSkillComparison.md): rc.9/rc.10 both yield useful caches and splits; downstream checks pass; cache tradeoffs differ. | Selected real Prompting tasks, one author per arm/scope. No general superiority. Focused context arm did not load GenerateAlternatives; do not attribute its layout to that procedure. |
+| Did the focused trigger repair establish benefit? | [Activation follow-up](ExperimentMemory20261107/Sources/Activation.md): actual read → comparison → implementation; 5/5 executor checks each; candidate classifier bytes higher. | rc.9 versus repaired candidate, not the separately updated efficiency installation. Supports activation/preservation on this task; loading and solution superiority remain unsupported. |
+| Should identical lesson packets receive more selector trials? | [Discriminating experiment](ExperimentMemory20261107/Sources/Discriminating.md): all three methods inspect identical packets and stop/reframe; repair outcomes also tie. | Historical checkpoint, not autonomous orchestration reliability. Compare delivered treatments before repeating. Ordinary-history versus common-packet question remains distinct; missing arm/transcript provenance stays unknown. |
+| Does an earlier failure mean the final target failed? | [Discriminating report audit history](ExperimentMemory20261107/Sources/Discriminating.md): first audit wrongly demanded PlanChange; corrected exposure audit preserves outcome scores. [Operational efficiency](ExperimentMemory20261107/Sources/OperationalEfficiency.md) preserves initial runtime limits. | Distinguish runner/checker execution from established target observations. Inspect original and corrected evidence; do not delete failures or infer outcomes from a process exit alone. |
+| Is a historical “uninstalled” recommendation current? | [Validation integration note](ValidationSummary.md): 2026-11-07 user-authorized draft integration supersedes deployment status only. | Old reports' trial-time decisions remain intact. Integration does not establish comparative benefit or validate untested combinations. Verify current source version separately when needed. |
+| Can compact workflow guidance claim general cost savings? | [Operational-efficiency results](ExperimentMemory20261107/Sources/OperationalEfficiency.md): matched useful outcomes tie; full-task token usage increased. | Distinguish shorter instructions from observed task cost. Use workload-specific outcomes and costs; unknown billing remains unknown. |
+
+Source copies are portable report-level evidence, not full raw trial provenance. [Source manifest](ExperimentMemory20261107/sources.json) gives original project-relative paths and SHA-256. Raw traces remain in the project; unavailable underlying evidence limits any stronger claim. These sources were chosen for the present reuse experiment, not a complete historical review.
